1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,028
Ah Caroline… come on in.

2
00:00:02,028 --> 00:00:02,860
Sit down.

3
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:04,000
Thanks.

4
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
So how's the dissertation planning going?

5
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,800
Well Dr Schulmann, I'm still having a lot of trouble deciding on a title.

6
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:11,850
Well,

7
00:00:11,850 --> 00:00:14,044
that's perfectly normal at this stage.

8
00:00:14,044 --> 00:00:17,570
And this is what your tutorials will help you to do.

9
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:18,130
Right.

10
00:00:18,130 --> 00:00:23,351
What we'll do is jot down some points that might help you in your

11
00:00:23,351 --> 00:00:23,724
decision.

12
00:00:23,724 --> 00:00:28,200
First of all, you have chosen your general topic area, haven't you?

13
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:30,600
Yes, it's the fishing industry.

14
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:31,365
Oh yes,

15
00:00:31,365 --> 00:00:34,425
that was one of the areas you mentioned.

16
00:00:34,425 --> 00:00:38,250
Now, what aspects of the course are you good at?

17
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:41,964
Well, I think I'm coping well with statistics,

18
00:00:41,964 --> 00:00:44,750
and I'm never bored by it.

19
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:46,630
Good, Anything else?

20
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:53,135
Well, I found computer modelling fascinating - I have no problem following what's being

21
00:00:53,135 --> 00:00:58,640
taught, whereas quite a few of my classmates find it difficult.

22
00:00:58,640 --> 00:00:58,995
Well,

23
00:00:58,995 --> 00:01:00,061
that's very good.

24
00:01:00,061 --> 00:01:04,680
Do you think these might be areas you could bring into your dissertation?

25
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:06,186
Oh yes, if possible.

26
00:01:06,186 --> 00:01:10,705
It's just that I'm having difficulty thinking how I can do that.

27
00:01:10,705 --> 00:01:14,470
You see I feel I don't have sufficient background information.

28
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:15,441
I see.

29
00:01:15,441 --> 00:01:17,870
Well, do you take notes?

30
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:20,162
I'm very weak at note-taking.

31
00:01:20,162 --> 00:01:23,370
My teachers always used to say that.

32
00:01:23,370 --> 00:01:28,034
Well, I think you really need to work on these weaknesses before you go

33
00:01:28,034 --> 00:01:28,700
any further.

34
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:29,970
What do you suggest?

35
00:01:29,970 --> 00:01:33,370
Well, I can go through the possible strategies with you

36
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:36,430
and let you decide where to go from there.

37
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:37,610
Okay, thanks.

38
00:01:37,610 --> 00:01:42,776
Well, some people find it helpful to organise peer-group discussions - you know, each

39
00:01:42,776 --> 00:01:48,340
week a different person studies a different topic and shares it with the group.

40
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:50,220
Oh right.

41
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:55,170
It really helps build confidence, you know, having to present something to others.

42
00:01:55,170 --> 00:01:56,310
I can see that.

43
00:01:56,310 --> 00:02:01,108
The drawback is that everyone in the group seems to share the same ideas…

44
00:02:01,108 --> 00:02:03,850
they keep being repeated in all the dissertations.

45
00:02:03,850 --> 00:02:04,830
Okay.

46
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:08,267
You could also try a service called 'Student Support'.

47
00:02:08,267 --> 00:02:13,614
It's designed to give you a structured programme over a number of weeks to

48
00:02:13,614 --> 00:02:14,760
develop your skills.

49
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:15,900
Sounds good.

50
00:02:15,900 --> 00:02:19,223
Yes, unfortunately there are only a few places.

51
00:02:19,223 --> 00:02:21,300
But it's worth looking into.

52
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:22,292
Yes, of course.

53
00:02:22,292 --> 00:02:25,600
I know I've got to work on my study skills.

54
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:29,640
And then there are several study skills books you can consult.

55
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:30,320
Right.

56
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:36,060
They'll be a good source of reference but the problem is they are sometimes

57
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:36,880
too general.

58
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:37,248
Yes,

59
00:02:37,248 --> 00:02:38,720
that's what I've found.

60
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:46,047
Other than that I would strongly advise quite simple ideas like using a card

61
00:02:46,047 --> 00:02:46,570
index.

62
00:02:46,570 --> 00:02:49,380
Well, yes, I've never done that before.

63
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:50,240
It's simple,

64
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:56,260
but it really works because you have to get points down in a small

65
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:56,690
space.

66
00:02:56,690 --> 00:03:01,052
Another thing I always advise is don't just take your notes

67
00:03:01,052 --> 00:03:02,638
and forget about them.

68
00:03:02,638 --> 00:03:07,000
Read everything three times - that'll really fix them in your mind.

69
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,740
Yes, I can see it'd take discipline but…

70
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:15,105
Well, if you establish good study skills at this stage they'll be with you

71
00:03:15,105 --> 00:03:16,040
all your life.

72
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,770
Oh yes, I completely agree.

73
00:03:17,770 --> 00:03:21,923
It's just that I don't seem to be able to discipline myself.

74
00:03:21,923 --> 00:03:24,000
I need to talk things over.

75
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:28,209
Well, we'll be continuing these tutorials of course.

76
00:03:28,209 --> 00:03:30,840
Let's arrange next month's now.

77
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:39,296
Let's see, I can see you virtually any time during the week starting 22nd

78
00:03:39,296 --> 00:03:39,900
January.

79
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:42,900
What about the 24th?

80
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:46,650
I'm free in the afternoon.

81
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:48,463
Sorry, I'm booked then.

82
00:03:48,463 --> 00:03:50,730
What about the following day?

83
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:51,242
Thursday?

84
00:03:51,242 --> 00:03:53,800
I can make the morning.

85
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:56,360
Fine, we'll go for the 25th then.

86
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,870
That's great, thanks.
